      "description": "Watch Stoke City vs Hull City highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The Carabao Cup delivered high-stakes drama on August 25, 2026, as Stoke City played host to Hull City . Both sides entered the fray with a place in the next round at stake, leading to a contest defined by tactical discipline and moments of individual brilliance. A Tale of Two Goals The match ignited in the first half with end-to-end action. Hull City threatened early through David Akintola , but Stoke goalkeeper Josh Griffiths produced several vital saves to keep the visitors at bay. The deadlock was eventually broken in the 39th minute by the home side. A pinpoint cross from Sorba Thomas found Róbert Bozeník , who clinicaly headed home from close range to give the Potters the lead. However, Hull City responded just before the interval. In the 45th minute, Liam Millar turned provider, setting up Kieran Dowell in the center of the box. Dowell unleashed a precise left-footed strike into the top left corner, ensuring the teams went into the break on level terms. Stalemate and Strategic Changes The second half saw a physical battle as both managers turned to their benches to find a breakthrough. Hull City dominated much of the possession, with Akintola and Kieran Dowell continuing to test the Stoke defense. The Potters suffered injury setbacks, losing Laurence Giani and Ben Pearson , which forced defensive reshuffling. Despite the pressure from the Tigers, including a late attempt from Tyrell Sellars-Fleming that sailed just over the bar, neither side could find a winner in regulation time. Shootout Decider With the score tied at 1-1 after 90 minutes, the match moved to a penalty shootout. Both teams displayed clinical finishing from the spot until the pressure mounted. The decisive moment arrived when Stoke's George Hirst saw his effort saved by Hull keeper Dillon Phillips . Mohamed Belloumi then stepped up to calmly convert the final penalty, securing a 5-4 shootout victory for Hull City and confirming their progression in the tournament."
