      "description": "Watch Stoke City vs Oldham highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The Carabao Cup fixture on 2026-08-08 brought together Stoke City and Oldham Athletic in a contest defined by tactical shifts and decisive second-half moments. Both sides entered the pitch with high energy, looking to secure a place in the next round of the competition. Defensive Resilience in a Goalless First Half Oldham Athletic started the match with intent, refusing to be overawed by their opponents. Within the opening ten minutes, Mike Fondop forced two smart saves from Viktor Johansson , signaling the visitors' threat. Stoke City gradually grew into the game, with Sam Gallagher becoming a central figure in their offensive efforts. Gallagher saw a close-range effort saved by Mathew Hudson and later sent a header just wide of the target following a precise cross from Eric-Junior Bocat . The first half remained a balanced affair, characterized by missed opportunities and solid goalkeeping. While Sorba Thomas and Lamine Cissé looked to spark creativity for the hosts, Oldham's defensive line, led by Donervon Daniels , held firm. The teams headed into the tunnel at halftime with the deadlock unbroken, setting the stage for a dramatic restart. Substitutions Turn the Tide for Stoke The momentum shifted shortly after the break when Stoke City took the lead in the 48th minute through an unfortunate own goal by Oliver Norburn . Oldham tried to find a way back, with Kane Drummond testing Johansson again in the 56th minute, but the hosts maintained their composure. A series of substitutions mid-way through the second half proved to be the turning point for Stoke . The introduction of Bae Jun-Ho and Róbert Bozeník added fresh impetus to the attack. In the 82nd minute, Bae Jun-Ho turned provider, sliding a perfectly weighted through ball to Róbert Bozeník , who clinically fired into the bottom right corner to double the lead. Despite late pressure from Oldham , including headed chances for Elliott Nevitt and Jamie Robson , Stoke City managed the closing stages effectively to secure a 2-0 victory."
